{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope: The question asked for the overall difference in conversion rates (email minus paid_search). The analyst reported a weighted, segment‑adjusted difference (-0.134) instead of the raw difference shown in the output (0.0698). This changes the estimand.",
    "Overreach: The answer makes a causal statement that the email campaign “reduced conversion rates,” despite the data being observational and the channel not being randomized. Adjusting for customer segment does not eliminate all confounding, so a causal claim is unwarranted."
  ]
